sequenceDiagram
    autonumber off
    actor Steward
    participant Page as Profile page and<br/>scoreboard page (proposed)
    participant Profile as Profile route<br/>GET /api/profile
    participant Metrics as ContributionMetrics<br/>(proposed)
    participant DB as Supabase DB<br/>form_responses, sites_pa,<br/>people

    Note over Steward,DB: Covers US 1.0.5. Proposed for Sprint 4. "(proposed)" = the step is not in the code today.<br/>Design: docs/user-model.md, "Gamification proposal". The metrics are calculated.<br/>No points table. people.activity_points stays unused. The acceptance tests of US 1.0.5 still name points.

    Note over Steward,DB: Metrics on a profile
    Steward->>Page: Open a profile
    Page->>Profile: fetch GET /api/profile?personId (exists)
    Profile->>DB: Count active reports that are not archived, and distinct sites (exists)
    Profile->>Metrics: getContributionMetrics(personId, period) (proposed)
    Metrics->>DB: Distinct sites_pa.ab_county of the reports (counties visited)
    Metrics->>DB: Distinct site types and subtypes (site variety, column not decided)
    Metrics->>DB: Sites where the person has the earliest active report (site explorer)
    DB-->>Metrics: Counts
    Metrics-->>Profile: Metrics
    Profile-->>Page: stats with the new metrics (proposed)
    Page-->>Steward: Show the metrics

    Note over Steward,DB: Scoreboard (top contributor)
    Steward->>Page: Open the scoreboard, choose a metric and all time or last year (proposed)
    Page->>Metrics: getScoreboard(metric, period) (proposed)
    Metrics->>Metrics: Read the caller from the session. Approved users only
    Metrics->>DB: Rank people by the metric, in one SQL query
    DB-->>Metrics: Ranked people
    Metrics-->>Page: Ranked list
    Page-->>Steward: Show the scoreboard

    Note over Steward,DB: The counts are calculated on each read, so no stored value can become incorrect.<br/>An archived or deactivated report does not count.<br/>Open questions for the client: what makes two sites "different",<br/>and if a report of a permanently deleted site still counts.
